<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Radhanpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1753 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Radhanpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Babi Pathan Nawabi state in northern Gujarat, founded by a Mughal officer on the edge of the Rann of Kutch.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawan-mard-khan">Kamal-ud-din Khan Babi</a>, known as Jawan Mard Khan, was a Mughal officer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> from the Babi family that also ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/junagadh-state">Junagadh State</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmedabad">Ahmedabad</a> in 1753 he secured Radhanpur and nearby districts as his own principality.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Nawabs ruled a dry territory on the trade route towards <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cutch-state">Kutch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>. Under British protection Radhanpur was an 11-gun salute state, first under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/palanpur-state">Palanpur</a> Agency and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-india-states-agency">Western India States Agency</a>, with a largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> farming population.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Radhanpur was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948 and has been part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> since 1960; it is now in Patan district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/radhanpur-state.jpg" alt="Radhanpur State" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Andreas Birken at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaurashtraKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1753 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century"